# Subly Project Rules

## Identity
Subly is Solana's commerce layer. We build on `solana-program/subscriptions` (audited by Cantina). Open-source core, hosted infrastructure.

## Two-Repo Architecture
- **PUBLIC** (`Subly_main/`): apps/, packages/, configs → github.com/Subly-Fi/Subly
- **PRIVATE** (`Subly_main/_internal/`): marketing/, docs/, session files → github.com/Subly-Fi/internal
- These are TWO separate git repos. `_internal/` is in the public repo's `.gitignore`.
- NEVER commit _internal/ content to the public repo.

## Session Protocol

### Start
1. Read `_internal/CLAUDE.md` → `_internal/TODO.md` → `_internal/DEVLOG.md`
2. Identify the current task from `_internal/TODO.md`
3. If DEVLOG.md has a "Next" item from the previous session, start there

### End (when user says "oturumu bitir", "session done", "wrap up")
1. Mark completed tasks in `_internal/TODO.md`, add new ones discovered during work
2. Append a session entry to `_internal/DEVLOG.md`
3. If structural changes happened, update `_internal/CLAUDE.md` and `_internal/docs/codebaseSummary.md`

## Monorepo Structure (Public)
- `apps/web` — Next.js 15 marketing site (subly.fi)
- `apps/merchant` — Merchant dashboard (Vite + React 19, forked from subscriptions webapp)
- `apps/api` — Hono backend API
- `packages/sdk` — @subly/sdk developer SDK
- `packages/ui` — @subly/ui embeddable components
- `packages/subscriptions` — Upstream reference (git subtree, DO NOT edit directly)
- `packages/config` — Shared tsconfig, eslint, tailwind

## Internal Structure (Private - _internal/)
- `_internal/marketing/` — Twitter, Telegram, brand, content
- `_internal/docs/` — Roadmap, tech stack, codebase summary
- `_internal/CLAUDE.md` — Project identity card
- `_internal/TODO.md` — Task tracker
- `_internal/DEVLOG.md` — Session log

## Development Standards
- TypeScript strict mode everywhere
- Test after every meaningful change
- Conventional Commits: feat:, fix:, refactor:, docs:, chore:
- Use early returns, max 2 levels nesting
- Extract functions longer than 30 lines
- Handle errors explicitly — never swallow them silently
- Name booleans with is/has/should prefix

## Language
- Code: English
- Comments: English
- User-facing conversation: Turkish
